<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    intersection.con.xml
    =====================
    12 explicit connections, exactly one per lane per approach (4
    approaches times 3 lanes). No lane carries more than one movement,
    which is the structural fix for the earlier shared-lane problem.

    Deliberately absent from this file: any tl or linkIndex attribute.
    Assigning controlled link indices before the network has actually been
    built and inspected would mean guessing at numbering that netconvert
    has not generated yet, exactly the mistake being corrected in this
    revision. Node C is still marked type="traffic_light" in
    intersection.nod.xml, so netconvert will automatically build controlled
    links for every one of these 12 connections and assign its own index
    order. That real, generated order is what gets inspected in NetEdit
    before any tlLogic is written.

    Lane discipline, identical on every approach:
      Lane 0 (kerb-side)   = LEFT turn only
      Lane 1 (middle)      = STRAIGHT only
      Lane 2 (median-side) = RIGHT turn only

    Target lane rule: each movement preserves its lateral position through
    the junction wherever geometrically reasonable, left arrives at the
    destination's lane 0, straight at lane 1, right at lane 2.

    No U-turn connections are defined.

    Movement geometry (from intersection.nod.xml, N=top, S=bottom, E=right,
    W=left):
      N_in (heading south)  : left to E, straight to S, right to W
      S_in (heading north)  : left to W, straight to N, right to E
      E_in (heading west)   : left to S, straight to W, right to N
      W_in (heading east)   : left to N, straight to E, right to S

    Whether the left turn connections actually stay clear of the opposing
    straight lane, rather than sweeping across it, depends on the real
    turning geometry netconvert computes from the corner radius and lane
    offsets. That must be checked visually in NetEdit once the network is
    built, it is not assumed here.
-->
<connections>
    <!-- North approach (N_in) -->
    <connection from="N_in" to="C_out_E" fromLane="0" toLane="0"/>  <!-- left -->
    <connection from="N_in" to="C_out_S" fromLane="1" toLane="1"/>  <!-- straight -->
    <connection from="N_in" to="C_out_W" fromLane="2" toLane="2"/>  <!-- right -->

    <!-- South approach (S_in) -->
    <connection from="S_in" to="C_out_W" fromLane="0" toLane="0"/>  <!-- left -->
    <connection from="S_in" to="C_out_N" fromLane="1" toLane="1"/>  <!-- straight -->
    <connection from="S_in" to="C_out_E" fromLane="2" toLane="2"/>  <!-- right -->

    <!-- East approach (E_in) -->
    <connection from="E_in" to="C_out_S" fromLane="0" toLane="0"/>  <!-- left -->
    <connection from="E_in" to="C_out_W" fromLane="1" toLane="1"/>  <!-- straight -->
    <connection from="E_in" to="C_out_N" fromLane="2" toLane="2"/>  <!-- right -->

    <!-- West approach (W_in) -->
    <connection from="W_in" to="C_out_N" fromLane="0" toLane="0"/>  <!-- left -->
    <connection from="W_in" to="C_out_E" fromLane="1" toLane="1"/>  <!-- straight -->
    <connection from="W_in" to="C_out_S" fromLane="2" toLane="2"/>  <!-- right -->
</connections>